 ### [3D Gaussian Splatting Training](3761-3d-gaussian-splatting-training.md)
-Non-deep-learning optimization process adjusting explicit 3D Gaussian parameters (centers, covariances, opacities, colors) using differentiable rasterization and adaptive density control.
+3D Gaussian Splatting (3DGS) training is a non-deep learning optimization process that adjusts the parameters of explicit 3D Gaussian primitives to minimize the difference between rendered images and ground truth images, using camera information and initial 3D Gaussian estimates. Unlike NeRF or Plenoxels, which optimize implicit neural fields, 3DGS training optimizes explicit geometric attributes (position, scale, rotation) and shading attributes (opacity, spherical harmonic coefficients). It sets itself apart from its siblings by using a differentiable rasterization-based forward model rather than ray-marching or neural volume evaluation, allowing for extremely fast training and rendering.
 
 ### [Refractive Index Tomography using Neural Fields](4146-refractive-index-tomography-using-neural-fields.md)
