+Refractive Index Tomography using Neural Fields (RNTF) is a method to recover a 3D refractive index field ($\eta$) and a luminance field from single-view refracted image measurements by optimizing neural fields that represent these quantities. It differs from standard NeRF-like methods by modeling the physical propagation of light through a medium with varying refractive index, requiring the integration of ray trajectories via Ordinary Differential Equations (ODEs) rather than fixed-step volumetric integration.
