+### [Radar Fields](8904-radar-fields.md)
+Radar Fields is a differentiable rendering framework that extends the radiance field concept to Synthetic Aperture Radar (SAR) imagery, enabling the learning of volumetric surface models from multiple SAR measurements. Unlike optical radiance fields that integrate emission along individual rays, Radar Fields integrates radar signal contributions across all rays within a given azimuth plane that share the same range distance. This architectural difference allows for the reconstruction of 3D geometry from SAR data, which offers day-night and cloud-penetrating imaging capabilities.
