 ### EndoNeRF
-A method for deformable surgical scene reconstruction using a canonical radiance field and a time-dependent displacement field, optimized with stereo depth-cueing and supervision. Radiance and density at point $\mathbf{x}$ at time $\tau$ are obtained by querying the canonical field $F_\theta$ at the displaced location: $F_\theta(\mathbf{x} + G_\phi(\mathbf{x}, \tau), \mathbf{d})$. It uses an MLP architecture with 8 fully connected ReLU layers, each with 256 channels. It optimizes an entire spatial-temporal field, resulting in significant time and resource consumption [S7].
+EndoNeRF is a method for deformable surgical scene reconstruction using a canonical radiance field and a time-dependent displacement field, optimized with stereo depth-cueing and supervision [S5]. Radiance and density at point $\mathbf{x}$ at time $\tau$ are obtained by querying the canonical field $F_\theta$ at the displaced location: $F_\theta(\mathbf{x} + G_\phi(\mathbf{x}, \tau), \mathbf{d})$ [S5]. The MLP architecture consists of 8 fully connected ReLU layers, each with 256 channels [S5]. A key pitfall is that EndoNeRF optimizes an entire spatial-temporal field, resulting in significant time and resource consumption [S5].
 
